    float deviation = fabs(reading - averageReadings[sensorId]);
    if (deviation > maxDeviations[sensorId]) {
        maxDeviations[sensorId] = deviation;
        printf("Sensor %d has a new maximum deviation of %.2f at time %ld\n", 
            sensorId, maxDeviations[sensorId], time(NULL));
    }

    if (deviation > threshold) { // Anomaly detected
        anomaliesCount[sensorId]++;
        printf("Anomaly detected on Sensor %d at time %ld\n", sensorId, time(NULL));
    }

    averageReadings[sensorId] = (averageReadings[sensorId] + reading) / 2.0; // Simple moving average

    pthread_mutex_unlock(&dataLock);
}
```

Please note that the code above doesn't handle network intermittency, missing data or out-of-order arrival of data as it is quite complex and depends on the specifics of your system. Also, this code assumes `threshold` to be defined elsewhere in your program.

The function processData could be called each time you receive new sensor data from any of your sensors. It checks if a minute has passed since the last update, and updates the statistics accordingly. 

Also, the example above does not implement an error handling system. In a real-world situation, you might want to add code to handle possible errors, such as when a function fails or when it receives incorrect input. You also might want to include more detailed logging or error reporting in your code.
