    Node* currentNode = *head;
    while (currentNode != NULL) {
        if (currentNode->session == targetSession) {
            if (currentNode->prev != NULL) currentNode->prev->next = currentNode->next;
            if (currentNode->next != NULL) currentNode->next->prev = currentNode->prev;
            else *head = currentNode->prev;  // If removed last node, update head

            free(currentNode);
        }

        currentNode = currentNode->next;
    }

    pthread_mutex_unlock(&targetSession->mutex);  // Unlock target session's mutex
}
```
This solution uses a doubly linked list to manage multiple sessions. It protects concurrent modifications from different threads with mutex locks and supports dynamic scaling of resources based on current load. However, it doesn't include the logging mechanism or garbage collection optimization mentioned in your task. You should implement these as per your specific requirements.
