['This is quite an extensive task and will take time to write out here. It involves multiple different components including a thread-safe hash table with timestamping, local caches per thread, dynamic configuration service, monitoring interface, eviction strategies, logging mechanism, etc. Below is the basic start of how you might design the cache structure in C:

```c
#include <pthread.h>
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <time.h>

typedef struct Entry {
    int key;
    long offset;
    time_t timestamp;
    pthread_rwlock_t lock; // Reader/Writer lock for concurrent read/write operations
} Entry;

Entry** cache; 
size_t size = 10000000; // Large enough to hold up to 10 million entries
pthread_mutex_t resizeLock = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER; // Mutex for dynamic resizing of the hash table

// Hash function
size_t hash(int key) {
    return (size_t)(key % size);
}

// Initialize cache
void initCache() {
    cache = malloc(sizeof(Entry*) * size);
    for(int i = 0; i < size; ++i) {
        cache[i] = NULL;
    }
}

// Insert an entry into the cache
void insert(int key, long offset) {
    size_t index = hash(key);

    // Use a mutex to ensure that only one thread can resize the cache at a time
    pthread_mutex_lock(&resizeLock);
    if(cache[index] == NULL || cache[index]->key != key) {
        Entry* entry = malloc(sizeof(Entry));
        entry->key = key;
        entry->offset = offset;
        entry->timestamp = time(NULL);
        pthread_rwlock_init(&entry->lock, NULL);

        cache[index] = entry;
    } else {
        // Key already exists, update the value and timestamp
        Entry* entry = cache[index];
        pthread_rwlock_wrlock(&entry->lock);
        entry->offset = offset;
        entry->timestamp = time(NULL);
        pthread_rwlock_unlock(&entry->lock);
    }
    pthread_mutex_unlock(&resizeLock);
}
``` 

The above is just a starting point. You would need to add the remaining components: dynamic configuration, local caches per thread, logging mechanism, and so on. Also, this code does not handle resizing of the cache when it gets full (i.e., it will crash once it fills up). A proper implementation would have to include such features.
