2. Collision Resolution: This is a simple hash function that uses modulo to resolve collisions. There are many other strategies like open addressing, chaining etc. which can be used based on the use case. 
```c
int hash_function(int key, int size) {
    return key % size;
}
```
3. Resizing: If the load factor exceeds a certain threshold, we double the size of the array and rehash all keys.
```c
void resize(hash_table* table, int newSize) {
    // Create new arrays with new size
    long* newOffsets = calloc(newSize, sizeof(long));
    int* newKeys = calloc(newSize, sizeof(int));
    record* newRecords = calloc(newSize, sizeof(record));

    // Copy old elements into new arrays
    for (int i = 0; i < table->size; i++) {
        int key = hash_function(table->keys[i], newSize);
        while (newKeys[key] != 0) {
            key = (key + 1) % newSize;
        }
        newOffsets[key] = table->offsets[i];
        newKeys[key] = table->keys[i];
        newRecords[key] = table->records[i];
    }

    // Free old arrays and replace with new ones
    free(table->offsets);
    free(table->keys);
    free(table->records);
    table->offsets = newOffsets;
    table->keys = newKeys;
    table->records = newRecords;
    table->size = newSize;
}
```
