["This is a complex task that involves several aspects of C programming. Below is a simple outline of how you might implement this function in pseudo-code. Please note that actual implementation may vary significantly depending on your specific needs and constraints. 

```c
#include <stdlib.h>
#include <time.h>
#include <pthread.h>
#include <signal.h>
#include <stdatomic.h>  // This is a C11 feature, make sure your compiler supports it.

// The session structure
typedef struct {
    char* user_id;
    time_t start_time;
    time_t end_time;
} Session;

// Global variables for managing sessions and locks.
Session** sessions = NULL;
pthread_mutex_t lock;
size_t session_count = 0;

void handle_session(const char* user_id) {
    // Lock the global sessions array to avoid race conditions.
    pthread_mutex_lock(&lock);

    // Check if the user has an existing session, 
    for (size_t i = 0; i < session_count; ++i) {
        if (!strcmp(sessions[i]->user_id, user_id)) {
            sessions[i]->end_time = time(NULL); // Update the end time.
            ++session_count;
            goto unlock;
        }
    }

    // If there is no existing session for this user, create a new one.
    Session* new_session = malloc(sizeof(Session));
    new_session->user_id = strdup(user_id);
    new_session->start_time = time(NULL);

    // Resize the sessions array and add the new session.
    sessions = realloc(sessions, (session_count + 1) * sizeof(Session*));
    sessions[session_count] = new_session;
    ++session_count;

unlock:
    pthread_mutex_unlock(&lock);
}
```
This function handles a session for the specified user. It first locks the global sessions array to avoid race conditions when multiple threads are accessing it concurrently, and then checks if there is an existing session for the user. If so, it updates its end time; if not, it creates a new session with the current time as start_time. After that, it unlocks the lock.
Please note: This code doesn't include error handling, logging mechanism integration, memory optimization or session purging strategy. You should implement these parts according to your requirements and constraints. 

