    pthread_mutex_lock(&mutex);
    if (hashTable[index] == NULL) {
        hashTable[index] = node;
    } else {
        Node* temp = hashTable[index];

        while (temp->next != NULL) {
            temp = temp->next;
        }

        temp->next = node;
    }
    pthread_mutex_unlock(&mutex);
}
```
Please note that this is a simplified version of the problem. The solution will depend on the specific requirements and constraints, including how to handle varying loads efficiently, how to track and limit the total number of records, how to implement thread safety without data races, etc.
